Keep the GitHub repository picker on screen and in place on phones.

The repo and branch comboboxes in the new-session form open a popover of a
search field and a list up to 18rem tall, about 330px in all. A phone has less
room than that both above and below the picker, so Radix flipped the popover
to the top and it ran off the top of the screen, search field first. Radix
also flips a popover whenever it stops fitting where it is, and checks again
on every size change, so the repository chip's popover and the comboboxes in
it jumped from side to side as the chip's popover grew with each repo added,
a list shrank as the search filtered it, and a phone's keyboard came and went.
Now each popover picks its side once, when it opens (below, unless there's too
little room below and more above), doesn't flip, and is capped at the room on
that side, 8px off the screen edges, so it shrinks and scrolls instead of
running off the screen or moving. Above its trigger, a combobox also keeps
the height it opened with, so the search field doesn't slide down as the list
filters. On touch screens the search field also isn't focused on open, so the
on-screen keyboard doesn't pop up and pan the page; tapping the field focuses
it. Desktop, with room to spare, is unchanged.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0005.

